# colcon output. Never commit these: a clone that arrives with somebody else's
# build tree half-satisfies the next `colcon build`, which then fails in ways
# that look like a code problem and are not. Also dirties the repo on every
# build.
ros2/build/
ros2/install/
ros2/log/
missions/__pycache__/
console/_experiment_panel_src.py*
console/last_error.log

# session debris - never part of the project
*.patch
*.bak
*.crdownload
.claude_commit_msg.txt
test_output.txt
Claude outputs/


# THE REFERENCE LIBRARY IS NOT SOURCE. About 100 MB of PDFs, most of them
# publisher copies that are not ours to redistribute, and git keeps every
# version of a binary forever - so one accidental commit makes the clone
# permanently 100 MB heavier and no `git rm` afterwards takes it back out.
#
# The papers live beside the repo (OneDrive, a shared drive, wherever) and
# what IS in version control is the thing that matters: SOURCES.md, which
# names each one and says exactly which table or equation is being relied on.
# A reader can find a paper from a citation. They cannot find a citation from
# a PDF sitting in a folder.
CommsEv_References/
Deadband_References/

